{
  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a sustained uptrend (e.g., >72 EUR) followed by a flat or slightly declining sentiment score, the model consistently overestimates future prices by 1.5 to 3.0 EUR due to ignoring immediate mean reversion pressure.",
    "The model exhibits significant lag in detecting sharp downward spikes; when true outcomes drop below 68 EUR within the first week of the forecast horizon, the model fails to adjust its trajectory and continues projecting a gradual rise or flatline.",
    "In periods where sentiment shifts from neutral (0.00) to negative (-0.25) while price is near historical highs, apply a correction factor of -1.0 to -1.5 EUR per day for the first 7 days of the forecast to counteract the model's inertia.",
    "The model systematically underestimates volatility during high-price regimes (above 73 EUR), assuming linear growth where actual outcomes show erratic swings between 62 and 71 EUR within the same 30-day window.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed signals (e.g., -0.25 followed by +0.50) while price is declining, the model's tendency to smooth out the path leads to an overshoot of the true low point by approximately 2-4 EUR."
  ]
}
